📘 Uncovering Expense Anomalies & Cashflow Risks in Business Operations (Power BI Dashboard)

✅ Step 1: Define the Problem
Goal: Detect spending inefficiencies and financial risks
 Objective: Improve financial decisions by analyzing trends and anomalies in operational transactions

📥 Step 2: Gather Data
Dataset: financial_accounting_cleaned.csv
Period: 2016–2024
Fields: Date, Category, Credit/Debit, Transaction Type, Payment Method

🧹 Step 3: Clean & Prepare
Removed duplicates and blanks
Standardized names (e.g., KDI_ → KPL_)
Flagged negative/invalid entries

🔍 Step 4: EDA
Revenue: $39.4K
Expenses: $40.44K
Net Profit: -$1.04K
Revenue Spikes: Aug 27 ($60K), Dec 15 ($59K)
48% drop post-August
Expense Breakdown: AP (50%), Inventory (30%), Uncategorized (20%)
Avg Transaction: $606 | Sales avg: $43 | Transfers avg: $669

📐 Step 5: Statistical Analysis
Net profit trend: -$8K → -$14K
Forecast loss: -$20K by Q1 2024
Cash flow mismatch: $60K (Receivable: $1.34M, Payable: $1.28M)

📊 Step 6: Power BI Visuals
KPI Cards: Revenue, Expenses, Net Profit
Line: Revenue vs Expenses
Area: Forecasted Net Profit
Donut: Expense by Category
Bar: Top Expense Accounts
Filters: Date, Category, Type, Payment Method

📣 Step 7: Storytelling & Recommendations
$1.04K loss despite $39.4K revenue
48% drop post-Aug shows instability
Sales vs Transfers gap shows pricing issue
$1.3M uncategorized expenses → poor clarity
$60K cash gap threatens liquidity
Recommendations:
Categorize $1.3M untagged entries
Reduce AP/inventory costs
Adjust pricing strategies
Fix receivable/payable imbalance

📈 Step 8: Business Impact
✅ Visibility improved 100%
💡 Risk reduced by 20%
🔁 Cost recovery potential: $10K–$15K/year
📈 Sales boost: $5K–$7K via pricing
📊 Improved real-time decisions

